<title>USA: Chrysler gets $232 mln tax break in Ohio-NYT.</title>
<headline>Chrysler gets $232 mln tax break in Ohio-NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp. won $232 million worth of tax breaks and other government incentives for building a Jeep assembly plant in Toledo, Ohio, the New York Times said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The plant will employ 4,900 workers -- 600 fewer than the existing plant in Toledo, the paper said.</p>
<p>Still, local officials said the area would have been financially devastated if Chrysler decided to relocate.</p>
<p>The company will spend $600 million to build and equip the new factory and another $600 million to refurbish an existing building on the site, the paper said.</p>
</text>
